rust-xpra (0.5.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low
  * Bump version to 0.5.0.

 -- Antoine Martin <antoine@xpra.org>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:02:46 +0700

rust-xpra (0.4.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low
  * 🔧 Platforms, build and packaging:
    ship a CycloneDX SBOM with every release binary
    cover the protocol layer with tests
  * ✨ Features:
    add `-v` to raise the log level
    send the local display size and per-monitor layout in the hello packet
    send monitor-relative coordinates with every position
    map server window positions back to local coordinates
    place new windows by their client area, not their frame
    handle interrupts gracefully —
    `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`/`SIGHUP` and the Windows console events tell the server why we are leaving
    fix the Super key, the dead keys and the non-ascii ones
    take the modifier names from the server's keymap
    detect the keyboard layout on Windows and allow `XPRA_KEYBOARD_LAYOUT` overrides
    name the shifted punctuation keysyms
    don't confine the pointer to override-redirect windows
    don't lock the cursor when it cannot be confined
    don't report the geometry of a minimized window
    scale windows on HiDPI displays, with `XPRA_DESKTOP_SCALING` to override the display's scale factor
    show the macOS Dock icon only while there is a window
    handle server-requested window resizes through `window-resized`
    honour window attention requests
    support transient and parent windows, modal dialogs and relative popup positioning —
    window ownership on MS Windows, macOS and X11; modal state on MS Windows and X11
    honour skip-taskbar on MS Windows and X11, and skip-pager on X11
    use the application's class and instance for window grouping on X11 and Wayland
    honour window types on X11
    honour sticky window state on X11
    apply window opacity on X11
    honour shaded window state on X11
    place windows on the server-requested workspace on X11
    set server-provided icon titles on X11
  * 🌈 Encodings:
    vectorise the draw blit
    present only the regions that changed
    handle JPEG and PNG draw decode errors
  * 🖧 Network:
    work with servers running without backwards compatibility —
    every packet is accepted under both its legacy and its current name, and nothing sent depends
    on the server's `BACKWARDS_COMPATIBLE` mode any more
    raise the minimum supported server version to 7.0
    fix draw acknowledgement packet compatibility
    advertise window forwarding in the `window` namespace
    handle the modern cursor packets
    handle the `encoding-set` packet
    don't ping a server that advertises no ping capability
    reply to pings under the current packet name
    advertise notifications under the current name too
    don't panic on a hash key the server did not send
    take the remote xpra executable path as `--remote-xpra=PATH`
    take the SSH command and its options as `--ssh=COMMAND`
    support PuTTY's Plink with non-default SSH ports
    send the keyboard layout in a `keyboard-config` packet
    report the client version in the hello packet
  * Documentation:
    document macOS support

 -- Antoine Martin <antoine@xpra.org>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 22:57:08 +0700

rust-xpra (0.3.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low
  * 🔧 Platforms, build and packaging:
    build on older distributions
    disable lto on Debian
    build from github releases
  * ✨ Features:
    mmap
  * 🖧 Network:
    verify SSL certificates by default, add `--ssl-insecure`
  * Documentation:
    include an interactive dependency graph
    link to repositories

 -- Antoine Martin <antoine@xpra.org>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 17:18:37 +0700

rust-xpra (0.3.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low
  * connection dialog when started without any arguments
  * system tray icon with an `Exit` menu entry (MS Windows)
  * show server notifications as tray balloons (MS Windows)
  * embed the application icon and the DPI-awareness manifest
    into the Windows executable
  * send the packet types introduced in xpra 6.5, which raises
    the minimum server version to 6.6
  * initial Debian packaging, with a rust-xpra(1) man page

